 "title": "Green's theorem on the unit circle",
 "caption": "Along the unit circle F = (−y, x) is a tangent vector of length 1, so ∮ (−y dx + x dy) = (length 1) × (circumference 2π) = 2π. Green's theorem gives the same: ∬ 2 dA = 2 × area π = 2π.",
 "alt": "The unit circle with four tangent arrows of the field (−y, x), all of length 1 and pointing anticlockwise, enclosing area π.",
 "description": [
  "On the circle, F = (−y, x) is tangent to the circle and has length 1.",
  "The circumference is 2π, so the line integral is 1 × 2π = 2π.",
  "Green: ∬ (∂Q/∂x − ∂P/∂y) dA = ∬ 2 dA = 2π, the same value."
